<!--
  Day 3 / 3.3 — Cross-component communication via m.global (XML half)

  Runs in: BrightScript Simulator (or real device).

  When two components are siblings (neither is the other's parent),
  passing data through interface fields would force the common parent
  to relay every message. m.global avoids that: it is a single
  scene-wide roSGNode every component sees as the same instance.

  Typical setup:
    1. The Scene's init() declares the shared fields ONCE:
          m.global.addField("currentMovieId", "integer", false)
          m.global.addField("appTheme",       "string",  false)
    2. Any component reads or writes them by name:
          m.global.currentMovieId = 42
    3. Any component subscribes from anywhere:
          m.global.observeField("currentMovieId", "onMovieChanged")

  m.global is essentially an EventBus the platform gives you for free.
  Keep it lean: SHARED app state only, not screen-local UI state.

  This demo writes its own component name plus a payload into a global
  "lastEmitter" field whenever simulateEmit() is called.
-->
<component name="CrossComponentDemo" extends="Group">
    <script type="text/brightscript" uri="pkg:/components/CrossComponentDemo.brs" />
</component>
